  ['What does Axis-Y Dark Spot Correcting Glow Serum do?', 'It is a lightweight daily serum aimed at dark spots, post-acne marks and uneven tone. The brand says it contains 5% niacinamide, squalane, glutathione, hyaluronate and several fruit extracts, and that it helps visibly reduce dark spots while supporting hydration.'],
  ['What are the ingredients in Axis-Y Dark Spot Correcting Glow Serum?', 'According to the brand’s own page, the list starts with water, glycerin and niacinamide, followed by sodium hyaluronate, propanediol, erythritol, butylene glycol and squalane. It also includes rice bran, calendula, papaya, sea buckthorn and acerola extracts, glutathione, allantoin and rosemary leaf oil. See the full list in the article.'],
  ['How long does it take to see results?', 'The brand reports a 20% reduction in the appearance of dark spots after 4 weeks in its own clinical evaluation, without sharing the study size or design. In my own use, I would give it at least 3 weeks of regular use. The reviewers I found describe it as gradual and mild, and the American Academy of Dermatology says spots a few shades darker than your skin tone usually take 6 to 12 months to fade once the cause is removed. I would plan on weeks to months, not days.'],
  ['Can I use it every day, morning and night?', 'It is described by the brand as lightweight and comfortable for daily use across skin types. Brand directions are to apply a small amount to the whole face or to targeted areas and pat it in. I prefer using it in the evening and leave the morning for another active. Start once a day and patch-test first, especially if your skin reacts to plant extracts or essential oils.'],
  ['Do I still need sunscreen with a dark spot serum?', 'Yes, and it matters more than the serum. The American Academy of Dermatology says daily sunscreen is the starting point for fading dark spots, because sun exposure keeps spots dark. My own favourite sunscreens are covered in my Round Lab sunscreen review.'],
